1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
I promise, I will make your wish come true.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Even if it means hurting someone else.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Even if it means hurting myself.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
But when your dream becomes reality,

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
there's something I must ask in return.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Please, no matter what, smile for me.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Please, no matter what, smile for me.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Please, no matter what, smile for me.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Fast.

10
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
At least for me.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
We are if you are still alive.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,960
実は人絵に カードの裏を持て 解けない

13
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:28,660
目めくりめくるなく 目まぐるしいステージで

14
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:36,840
その絡まった感情 満足いくまで何回も

15
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:39,960
壊してしまう

16
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:44,280
運命に手招きされ彷徨う明日は

17
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:50,600
何を選んで何を手放し一つになればいいんだろう

18
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:56,100
馴染った手札を晒く余裕なんてないよ

19
00:01:56,100 --> 00:02:00,440
乾いた後悔の海を飲み越す君は

20
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:06,540
限られた言葉でいつしかの笑顔を許してほしいんだろう

21
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:11,560
現実を忘れたって構わないよ

22
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:16,980
だから今も知らないでいたいな

23
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:28,020
For real? Iona plays Wecross too?

24
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:32,760
Yeah, so? Wecross is fun!

25
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,540
Even I bought a starter deck.

26
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,220
I thought it was a guy thing.

27
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:37,960
But whatever, I guess.

28
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:37,980
Whatever, I guess.

29
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:08,540
Hello, Ruko. Welcome home.

30
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:23,960
Hey, Grandma!

31
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,960
Hey, Grandma!

32
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,380
Hey, Grandma!

33
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,380
Hello, Ruko! Welcome home!

34
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,380
Hey, Grandma!

35
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:35,380
Hey, Grandma!

36
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:42,420
Just leave your bag on the floor there, it's cool.

37
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:42,640
pay off to me, everyone's face!

38
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,800
Okay, get off.

39
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,720
Hold on.

40
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,000
It's kinda high-claring stuff on that day.

41
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,500
Long time no see.

42
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,340
If you say so.

43
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,100
What's up, Grandma?

44
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,980
Yeah, just leave your bag on the floor there.

45
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:56,520
It's cool.

46
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,560
Well, that's that.

47
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,440
It's an apartment building after all.

48
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,260
Grandma wins this round.

49
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:11,480
Man, I thought it was going to be an office for sure.

50
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:14,560
Now I've got to clean the bathroom for a whole week.

51
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:19,180
Either way, one more pillar is all they need to finish the puzzle.

52
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,700
Puzzle? What do you mean?

53
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:26,060
Just think about how many points they'll get when they drop a pillar into that alley over there.

54
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:28,360
Oh.

55
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,380
They're only one building away from a Tetris.

56
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:44,540
And then the whole city might just disappear on us.

57
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:48,840
Finally!

58
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:53,560
Jeez, Grandma, these levels you make are getting way too hard for me.

59
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:56,020
Suppose I'd better start on dinner.

60
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:57,480
Oh, let me help you.

61
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:59,760
You've hardly been home for five minutes.

62
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:01,920
Why don't you relax a bit with your brother?

63
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:05,660
Or maybe you can get a start on bathroom cleaning duty.

64
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:07,140
Oh, no.

65
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,040
Nah.

66
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:10,420
I think I'd rather bother you.

67
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:15,820
Ew!

68
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,700
Would it kill you to take off your socks?

69
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:20,060
Now it stinks in here!

70
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:20,580
Yeah?

71
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,440
No!

72
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,660
You're going to give me the plague or something!

73
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,160
I want to go help with dinner!

74
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:28,200
It's always a party with Ayumu around.

75
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,300
Yeah, like the stinkiest party ever!

76
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:36,320
Come all the way out here just to hang with me?

77
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,500
You must really look up to your big bro.

78
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:40,760
No way!

79
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:42,900
I just came to get some milk tea.

80
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:44,940
Only one vending machine has my favorite.

81
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:48,980
Listen, try not to worry Grandma so much, okay?

82
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,200
I'm worrying her?

83
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:52,400
Yeah, a little.

84
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:56,260
She was telling me earlier that you haven't made any friends since you switched schools.

85
00:05:56,780 --> 00:06:00,020
But it's not like I really need friends to be happy.

86
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:03,220
Well, you're not exactly shy, so I'm sure you'll meet someone.

87
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,360
But you know how Grandma can be.

88
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:07,780
She's always trying to look out for us.

89
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:12,640
Here.

90
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:14,260
What's that?

91
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:15,560
Just open it.

92
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:19,800
It's this card game a buddy from work told me about.

93
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:22,140
He said it's crazy popular with girls your age.

94
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:23,640
I don't know, I thought it might be fun.

95
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:26,620
Yeah, I think I've seen some girls in class playing this.

96
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,060
Well, there you go.

97
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:28,720
Perfect.

98
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,800
Now you have a secret weapon to make friends.

99
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:41,820
I didn't realize I was worrying Grandma so much.

100
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:42,720
See ya!

101
00:06:44,260 --> 00:07:03,360
Was it chilly out there?

102
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:08,840
Cold, cold, cold, go away.

103
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,040
Warm, warm is here to stay.

104
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,320
I'm, uh...

105
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:18,700
I'm gonna go study.

106
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:29,080
Friends or no friends.

107
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,940
I don't want Grandma to worry about me all the time.

108
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:35,960
I guess it wouldn't hurt to give this a look at least.

109
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:39,340
Let's see here.

110
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:42,580
One of the cards is called an L-Rig and works as the player's avatar.

111
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:45,080
This one, maybe?

112
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,260
She's so cute!

113
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:51,760
Okay, so when it's the player's turn, this card will...

114
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,760
Hmm...

115
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:58,700
Oh, her voice is cute, too!

116
00:07:59,260 --> 00:07:59,480
What?

117
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:00,680
Huh?

118
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:16,780
I heard a crash.

119
00:08:16,780 --> 00:08:18,680
Oh no, are you hurt?

120
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,080
No, no, I'm okay.

121
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:25,400
Did you fall out of your chair?

122
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:28,340
Wait, you don't hear that voice?

123
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:29,380
What voice?

124
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:34,400
I know this isn't just in my head.

125
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,560
Uh, anyway, I'm fine.

126
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:37,380
You can go now.

127
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:40,800
I need to get back to studying, so, uh, why don't you take the first bath tonight?

128
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,000
Rue, wait.

129
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:42,700
But be careful.

130
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:44,840
Make sure the water's nice and warm.

131
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:46,420
Don't catch a cold, okay?

132
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:47,760
Fine, fine.

133
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,660
Good night.

134
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:37,340
You can't disappear!

135
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:40,960
Oh no, no, no, no, no.

136
00:09:40,960 --> 00:10:10,940
Oh, my God.

137
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:13,540
Bet you were the one giving me weird dreams.

138
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,380
What the heck are you, anyway?

139
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:24,000
Cards aren't supposed to talk.

140
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:24,280
Battle!

141
00:10:25,420 --> 00:10:26,020
Battle?

142
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:29,000
So, you mean like a card battle thingy?

143
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:53,380
You don't need food, do you?

144
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:54,580
I mean, you're made of paper.

145
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,740
The broth would get you all wet and gross.

146
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:57,060
Battle!

147
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:57,380
Battle!

148
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:57,940
Oh!

149
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,920
You still want to play, huh?

150
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:10,820
Do I just, like, ask them?

151
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:15,600
I wonder if they could hear you,

152
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,580
because I don't think the other girls' cards can talk.

153
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:18,720
I don't get this.

154
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:19,520
I found you!

155
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:20,300
Huh?

156
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:26,060
Um, hi?

157
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:27,040
I knew it!

158
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,060
You're a selector!

159
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,700
I don't know that word.

160
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,480
Aha!

161
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:33,560
Who's your Elrig?

162
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:34,160
Huh?

163
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,720
So I'm not crazy?

164
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,980
You can hear her voice, too?

165
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:38,020
Course I can!

166
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:39,740
Here, look.

167
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,980
I have an Elrig just like you.

168
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,180
Her name's Hario.

169
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:46,720
Now, on guard!

170
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,580
Yeah, I don't get this.

171
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:57,500
Perfect!

172
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,880
We've got the whole roof to ourselves!

173
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,380
Your card can speak, like real sentences,

174
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,120
but mine is kind of not quite there.

175
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:09,640
She, well, mostly just makes these little cat noises.

176
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:10,600
Ruko, right?

177
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,820
Kazuki, that is super cool.

178
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,460
You can hear all the Elrigs, too.

179
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,260
Huh?

180
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,220
I still don't get how that works.

181
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:18,260
Yeah, it's weird.

182
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:20,000
Only selectors can hear them.

183
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:21,380
But it's okay,

184
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:23,700
since Yuzuki fills me in on what Hanio is saying.

185
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:25,280
That word again.

186
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,520
Here, let me explain.

187
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:28,800
There are some players,

188
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,560
specially chosen ones,

189
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:32,420
who get to compete to become the Eternal Girl.

190
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:33,100
Wait.

191
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:34,720
Compete for what?

192
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,000
If you become the Eternal Girl,

193
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,580
your one true wish will be granted,

194
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:40,100
and you can make it happen just by winning enough battles.

195
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:42,700
Your wish will come true just like magic?

196
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,520
Well, that's what they say.

197
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,460
That's a bit of an oversimplification.

198
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:48,360
More precisely,

199
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:51,620
the Eternal Girl is someone with the power to make dreams come true.

200
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:52,840
If cards can talk,

201
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,320
then maybe anything could happen.

202
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:57,160
I admit it does sound like pure fantasy,

203
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,760
granting wishes and all that.

204
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:00,160
However,

205
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:02,760
these cards have the power without a doubt.

206
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:05,800
So long as you are able to triumph in battle,

207
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,360
you can make anything a reality.

208
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:10,020
That doesn't apply to all players, though.

209
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:12,800
Only selectors have living Elrigs like me.

210
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:14,580
You are different.

211
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,920
You are the chosen ones.

212
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:19,820
Perhaps you've noticed this yourself,

213
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,680
but several celebrities have announced

214
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:23,060
they're playing Wee Cross as well.

215
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:26,420
Since there's no easy way to find and identify other selectors,

216
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:28,440
it's possible they're trying to use the media

217
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,600
to draw out competitors.

218
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,060
Really?

219
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:33,820
There is one last thing you must know.

220
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:36,240
If you lose three battles,

221
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,560
you also lose your right to be a selector.

222
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:39,680
How is that?

223
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,820
The moment you lose your third battle,

224
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:43,020
we disappear.

225
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:44,520
Needless to say,

226
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:45,860
no wishes will be granted.

227
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:48,400
And even if you picked up the cards again,

228
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,200
your life would never be the same.

229
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,580
Cool story, Hanayo.

230
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:52,860
Thanks a bunch.

231
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:53,840
Now let's battle.

232
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,020
Wait, I...

233
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,180
I don't even have a wish yet.

234
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:58,900
Who cares?

235
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:00,400
You don't need one to battle.

236
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:01,700
We can still have fun.

237
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:02,300
Battle!

238
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:03,400
Battle!

239
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:04,940
Battle now!

240
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:05,320
See?

241
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:06,560
Listen to your Elrig.

242
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:07,980
Come on, just one match.

243
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:09,540
Okay then.

244
00:14:09,860 --> 00:14:10,640
What's the harm?

245
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:11,720
There you go.

246
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:12,380
Yuzuki,

247
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,340
don't pressure her into a match.

248
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:16,020
She hasn't even learned the rules yet.

249
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,260
I'm playing to win.

250
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:18,600
If she sucks at this,

251
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,360
it just makes things easier for me.

252
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:20,980
Open!

253
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:21,020
Open!

254
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:32,260
Where are we?

255
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:50,300
Where are we?

256
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:51,500
What happened?

257
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,760
How did you...

258
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,320
Battle!

259
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:56,980
Hold on.

260
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:00,720
Yuzuki, Hanayo!

261
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:06,560
Hell yeah.

262
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:07,940
And I get to go first.

263
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,020
Okay, Rugo,

264
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,180
it's your turn now.

265
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,860
That's nice,

266
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,220
but I still don't know how to play.

267
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:18,380
Can you hear me?

268
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:20,540
Kazuki!

269
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,720
The rules are pretty easy.

270
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:27,200
Just summon a signi,

271
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:28,760
call out the name of your Elrig,

272
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,380
then launch your attack.

273
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:31,360
Kazuki!

274
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:32,800
Cut it out!

275
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,560
Whose side are you on here anyway?

276
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:35,900
For the last time,

277
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:37,760
people on the outside can't hear you.

278
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:38,780
What's her name?

279
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:39,680
Oh,

280
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:40,680
I don't know.

281
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:42,060
Let's see.

282
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:46,840
Uh,

283
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,020
Tama?

284
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,240
Why Tama?

285
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:51,440
I know it's dumb,

286
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,620
but she's always meowing,

287
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:54,220
and I used to have a cat named Tama,

288
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,100
so...

289
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:55,580
Tama!

290
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:58,140
Here goes nothing.

291
00:15:58,920 --> 00:15:59,640
Level one,

292
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:00,000
Gro!

293
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:01,900
Summoning a signi!

294
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:03,320
Tama attack!

295
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:05,540
Tama!

296
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:12,620
Ba-boom!

297
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,420
Was that bad?

298
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:17,240
I mean,

299
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:17,820
it's gone!

300
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:18,980
Did I break it or something?

301
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:20,400
Relax,

302
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,520
it's only a game.

303
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:22,980
As soon as the battle ends,

304
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:23,940
it'll be good as new.

305
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:25,040
It comes back?

306
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:25,580
Oh,

307
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:26,620
that's good.

308
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,100
Dang it, Kazuki!

309
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:29,340
This is all your fault!

310
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:30,560
If I don't win this,

311
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,120
I swear I'll pound your face in!

312
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:33,340
You can hear me,

313
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:33,980
right, Yuzuki?

314
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:35,160
I'm sorry,

315
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,460
but this is just wrong.

316
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,740
I want you to win,

317
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,160
but battles are supposed to be fair and square,

318
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:41,500
right?

319
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,480
If you have to do something underhanded

320
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,620
to make your wish come true,

321
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,400
will you really be happy in the end?

322
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:48,360
Level three,

323
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:48,940
Gro!

324
00:16:55,040 --> 00:17:00,080
That's fun!

325
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,280
She's so happy.

326
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:04,940
Battle more!

327
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,200
Why?

328
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:09,720
If this is really her first battle,

329
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:10,940
why is she so strong?

330
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:12,300
If this keeps up, I...

331
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:13,220
Calm down, Yuzuki.

332
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:15,340
You can't give up after just one turn.

333
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:16,940
No, you're right, but...

334
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:17,920
Oh, get it together!

335
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,660
If you want your wish to come true,

336
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,600
and Kazuki to...

337
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:20,760
No!

338
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,640
I told you,

339
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,060
don't say that out loud!

340
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:25,800
Honey, yo,

341
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,340
come on!

342
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:26,880
Set up the game!

343
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:27,320
Hurry!

344
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:27,380
Hurry!

345
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:38,200
What are you kids doing?

346
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,080
Lunch break is over!

347
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:41,500
Get back to class,

348
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:42,420
or I'll write you up!

349
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:43,280
Yes, sir!

350
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:45,700
Wait, so now what happens?

351
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,240
Was the battle a win or a loss?

352
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:51,220
If an external influence terminates the battle,

353
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:52,520
losses are not counted.

354
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,100
We call it a no-gamer.

355
00:17:54,660 --> 00:17:55,000
Good.

356
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:56,420
I was scared.

357
00:17:56,820 --> 00:17:57,740
Yeah, so...

358
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:58,400
your wish?

359
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,180
Let's go, Kazuki!

360
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:01,840
Bye, I guess!

361
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:06,540
Okay.

362
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,140
That was weird.

363
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:10,420
What do you think?

364
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:11,380
Huh, Tama?

365
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:16,760
Oh, she's been out cold

366
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,800
since the battle ended.

367
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:20,200
She really is super cute,

368
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:20,760
isn't she?

369
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:24,680
Well, most of the time.

370
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,580
They use up all of their power

371
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:33,040
in battle.

372
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:35,560
When it's over,

373
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:36,680
they usually just sleep.

374
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,000
Hanayo's the same.

375
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,620
Oh, I see.

376
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:44,400
So, uh...

377
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,740
Kazuki's not with you anymore?

378
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:47,160
Just because we're twins

379
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,060
doesn't mean we're connected

380
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:48,700
at the hip.

381
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:51,020
Listen,

382
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:52,580
could you not tell anyone

383
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,080
about what Hanayo said earlier?

384
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,080
Said about what?

385
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,320
You trying to make fun of me?

386
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:57,680
I really don't know

387
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,320
what you mean!

388
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:05,400
Hey, uh...

389
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:06,620
If you're not too busy,

390
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:07,900
you wanna...

391
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:08,420
hang out?

392
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:13,280
Oh, Ru, you're home.

393
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:14,860
And you brought a friend.

394
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,440
Hi, nice to meet you.

395
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:17,880
You don't mind

396
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,040
if we hang out here, do you?

397
00:19:19,260 --> 00:19:20,180
Of course not.

398
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:21,140
In fact,

399
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,500
I need to step out for a bit.

400
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:24,740
Help yourself to rice crackers.

401
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:28,020
Huh?

402
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:31,160
Well, don't I feel dumb?

403
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:32,400
It's funny.

404
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:34,220
Oh, I thought you must have

405
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:35,560
heard what she said for sure.

406
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:38,040
No, I don't think I did.

407
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,360
Oh, I was flipping out

408
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:39,960
over nothing.

409
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:41,000
Totally.

410
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,180
I'm guessing it was your wish,

411
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,300
Hanayo said.

412
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,900
Sorry, being nosy.

413
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:47,300
Yeah.

414
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:51,180
It's something I want

415
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,400
to come true no matter what.

416
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,680
But it's not the kind of wish

417
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:55,860
someone can make happen,

418
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:57,200
like with a bunch of hard work

419
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:57,700
or whatever.

420
00:19:58,420 --> 00:19:59,460
That's all I'll say.

421
00:20:00,080 --> 00:20:00,960
I understand.

422
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:03,100
I had given up, of course.

423
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,580
But when I met Hanayo

424
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:05,660
and became a selector,

425
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,580
she told me that even miracles

426
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:08,740
aren't beyond my reach.

427
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:10,520
And I want to believe her.

428
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,560
I want to believe that I can win

429
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:13,780
and become the Eternal Girl.

430
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:14,900
To have the power

431
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:16,000
to make my wish come true.

432
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:17,460
And all you have to do

433
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:18,240
is win, huh?

434
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,800
Well, okay then.

435
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:21,900
Let's have a card battle.

436
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:22,780
Only this time,

437
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:23,940
I'll lose on purpose, cool?

438
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:25,360
I'm not interested

439
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:27,320
in this Eternal Girl thing anyways.

440
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:28,580
No thanks.

441
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:29,500
I'll pass.

442
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:31,420
If Kalsuki ends up hating me,

443
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:32,740
then there's no point.

444
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:34,720
It defeats the purpose of my wish.

445
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:35,160
Hmm?

446
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,440
What does that mean?

447
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:38,180
Nothing.

448
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:41,160
Tea time, ladies!

449
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:42,900
Back already?

450
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:44,700
Rice crackers are a sorry snack

451
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:45,280
for you girls,

452
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:46,360
so I picked up something

453
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:47,320
a little more tasty.

454
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,000
Ooh, treats!

455
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,780
Wow, cake and macarons

456
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:52,980
and Bavarian cream?

457
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:54,960
Grandma, this is nuts!

458
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:55,960
There's no way

459
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:56,940
we can get all of this.

460
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:57,540
Thanks a bunch!

461
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:02,120
Oh my gosh, it's so good!

462
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:03,420
All of it is just amazing!

463
00:21:04,340 --> 00:21:05,360
Glad to hear it.

464
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:06,900
Why didn't you tell me

465
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:08,260
you had such a nice friend, Ru?

466
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:17,120
Now I'm all recharged.

467
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:17,860
See you later!

468
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,200
Yeah, see ya!

469
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:24,620
I don't know too much

470
00:21:24,620 --> 00:21:25,740
about Wee Cross yet,

471
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:26,760
and to be honest,

472
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:28,160
it all seems kind of scary.

473
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:30,700
But it's thanks to you,

474
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:31,740
Grandma so happy.

475
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,600
I'm glad I met you.

476
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:39,120
Ru Han, dinner's ready!

477
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:40,620
Coming!

478
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:43,740
Oh, I, uh, wanted to show you something.

479
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:45,000
What's that?

480
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,780
Actually, Yuzuki wasn't the only friend

481
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:49,440
I made today.

482
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:50,980
There's one more.

483
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:53,100
Her name's Tama.

484
00:21:53,100 --> 00:22:03,920
時計時影の影に

485
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,900
うなずいたら

486
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:08,580
終わりのボアが

487
00:22:08,580 --> 00:22:11,380
開き始まる闇

488
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:14,380
危うい答え

489
00:22:14,380 --> 00:22:17,100
そこに見え隠れる

490
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:20,240
今日の祈りは

491
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:21,140
明日

492
00:22:21,140 --> 00:22:23,940
多分になる

493
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:26,960
天と地を映す

494
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:29,600
逆さまの迷路

495
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:32,700
回り出した

496
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:33,940
歯車

497
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:38,640
人混みの中で

498
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:41,100
耳を澄ましたら

499
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:44,740
魂を招く

500
00:22:44,740 --> 00:22:47,140
あの鈴の音

501
00:22:47,140 --> 00:22:51,280
響く空へ

502
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:56,580
無限の果てまでは

503
00:22:56,580 --> 00:22:58,840
進むしかない

504
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:02,280
自分で選んだ

505
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:04,300
未来だから

506
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:08,200
届かない今すぐも

507
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:10,900
揺れる太陽を

508
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:13,940
いつか取り戻す

509
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:17,500
笑顔の場所

